   398	
   399	- Let S be the chosen dependency, e_P := e_P(S), E := E(S) (even), and γ⁻ := ∏_{e_P<0} z_P^{|e_P|}.
   400	- ψ is a ring homomorphism on Z[β], so ψ(η)² = ψ(Γ_S) = ψ(g′(β))²·∏_P ψ(z_P)^{|e_P|}.
   401	- Hence, with Y as in step 5,
   402	  Y² = q_S·t^{−E}·∏_P ψ(z_P)^{|e_P|}/ψ(γ⁻)² = q_S·t^{−E}·∏_P ψ(z_P)^{e_P} ≡ ∏_{i∈S} r_i² (mod N) by (1.1).
   403	- **Units.**
   404	  - ψ(z_P) = tG(P)/g₁ is a unit: G(P) = σℓn, with n B-smooth, and ℓ ∤ N, otherwise a factor was found.
   405	  - ψ(g′(β)) = t^{d−2}f′(g₀/g₁) is a unit by the field check (§4).
   406	  - √q_S involves only g₁ and primes ≤ B.
   407	- No map on K^× is needed. Every identity is a ring identity in Z[β] or in Q, followed by reduction mod N.
   408	- E1 checks this exactly: 0 violations in 116 cases.
   409	- **Final rational square root.** √q_S is computed from the recorded exponent vectors (halving), with
   410	  M_rows·k·(log N)^{O(1)} operations. No square root mod N is ever extracted.
