   275	  matters only for k < (d²−1)/4.
   276	- *Algorithm.*
   277	  1. Field selection (codex repair, replacing an ill-posed pilot and then a guess-and-double that
   278	     could waste a main-scale factor).
   279	     - Sample fresh fields, one capped descent attempt each, until an attempt succeeds. Keep that field.
   280	     - With q_A the per-attempt success probability and μ = E_A q_A, the kept field has law ∝ q_A, so
   281	       E[1/q_A | kept] = Pr(q_A > 0)/μ ≤ 1/μ.
   282	     - Thus C further successes cost C/μ attempts in expectation.
   283	     - By (i) and S′, μ ≥ (γ/2)^{2k+1}L^{−o(1)}.
