   297	  - The rational cofactor is (a − bm)/ℓ = N^{s − 1/(4k) + o(1)}.
   298	  - F(a, b) = N^{s + h + d/(4k) + o(1)}, where H = N^h is the coefficient height of R_A.
   299	  - The level-½ condition |a − bm| ≤ |F|^{1/2−η} is used by FM (§4). It needs h > s − (d−2)/(4k) + 2η.
   300	  - Adding the rational and algebraic sizes gives θ(d,k) + O(η).
   301	- θ(d,k) ↓ 3s as k → ∞.
   302	  - The displayed limits are infima over growing *fixed* k (codex); they are not attained at any
