   112	
   113	"L^{o(1)}" means exp(o(Λ)). Fixed powers L^ε and N^{o(1)} are not L^{o(1)}.
   114	
   115	**Parameters.** Fix:
   116	- odd d ≥ 3, k > (d+1)/4, a > 0, a compact σ-range, η₀ > 0;
   117	- a base exponent μ with ν + η₀ ≤ μ < 1 (μ = s is pcest's choice);
   118	- h ≥ h_*(μ) + η₀, where
   119	    h_*(μ) := max(2ν [Kern], μ − (d−2)ν [FM level ½], 1 − dμ + ν [window]);
   120	- H := ⌊N^h⌋, M := ⌊N^μ⌋, and W := ⌈N^{μ+ν+η₀/2}⌉.
   121	
   122	Then θ = θ_μ := (μ − ν) + (μ + h + dν) = 2μ + h + (d−1)ν. For μ = s, h_*(s) = s + ν and θ = 3s + dν.
